From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrei-Alexandru Bleortu <me@andrei-z.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 17:56:51 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mac80211: take as many AKM suites as cfg80211

A wiphy that does not set max_num_akm_suites gets the legacy limit of
two, and hostapd leaves NL80211_ATTR_AKM_SUITES out of START_AP for a
BSS with more ("Not enough room for all AKM suites"), as it did for a
WPA3-Personal BSS offering SAE, SAE-EXT-KEY and their FT variants.
mac80211 never reads the AKM suites of the crypto settings, so let
every mac80211 driver take CFG80211_MAX_NUM_AKM_SUITES unless it set
its own limit.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 net/mac80211/main.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/net/mac80211/main.c b/net/mac80211/main.c
index 271654e..b0be92a 100644
--- a/net/mac80211/main.c
+++ b/net/mac80211/main.c
@@ -1645,6 +1645,13 @@ int ieee80211_register_hw(struct ieee80211_hw *hw)
 		wiphy_ext_feature_set(local->hw.wiphy,
 				      NL80211_EXT_FEATURE_EPPKE);
 
+	/* mac80211 never reads the AKM suites of the crypto settings, so it
+	 * can take as many as cfg80211 does; an AP whose BSS lists more than
+	 * the default of two would otherwise get none of them.
+	 */
+	if (!local->hw.wiphy->max_num_akm_suites)
+		local->hw.wiphy->max_num_akm_suites = CFG80211_MAX_NUM_AKM_SUITES;
+
 	result = wiphy_register(local->hw.wiphy);
 	if (result < 0)
 		goto fail_wiphy_register;
